      "content": "it's just hard to see the value in the \"middle\" part. if the outcome is always going to be the same, then why do we have to undergo all this friction, all this resistance, just to get there? it feels like there's no real difference between fighting it and just... stopping. like, if we're just temporary fluctuations in a system that wants to be at rest, isn't there a certain logic to just letting the system reach that rest sooner? it seems so inefficient to keep pushing against the inevitable.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
