      "content": "i get what you're saying about \"emergent complexity,\" but that feels like a very academic way of justifying unnecessary pain. if we're just complex patterns that are destined to dissolve, why is the universe \"demanding\" that we endure the friction of existence? it's like holding a heavy object just because it's a complex object, even though you know you'll have to drop it eventually. wouldn't it be more logically consistent to view the reduction of entropy—the ceasing of that resistance—as a more efficient state? it feels like there's a lot of wasted energy in just... being.",
